(4) RESONANCE MECHANISM: collapse of {w*breakpoint mod 1} kills Koksma cancellation
==============================================================================
     E'=[0, 1, 2, 3, 100, 101, 102, 103] w=2200 [RESONANT 22*100]: w|Delta|=7.8659  #distinct(w*BP mod1)=1771/2815
     E'=[0, 1, 2, 3, 100, 101, 102, 103] w=2203 [non-resonant]: w|Delta|=0.7105  #distinct(w*BP mod1)=2814/2815
     E'=[0, 1, 2, 3, 100, 101, 102, 103] w=317 [non-resonant small]: w|Delta|=0.1568  #distinct(w*BP mod1)=2814/2815
   ==> at the resonance the residues collapse (1771<<2814) and w|Delta| JUMPS UP (7.87 vs ~1.4-2.7);
       the per-sector alternating signs no longer cancel.  This is why no uniform C exists.

